Reproducibility and Validation

Reproducibility Expectations

A run is considered reproducible if the script executes from a clean environment using the provided requirements and produces outputs with consistent structure and meaning.

Some numerical variation is expected due to stochastic elements unless random seeds are fixed.

Validation Layers

The pipeline includes multiple validation mechanisms:

ON vs OFF window comparison to test event locality

Phase-scrambled nulls to test phase dependence

Segment-shuffled nulls to test temporal ordering

Monte Carlo null estimation from observed ratio distributions

Classifier separation of real vs null segments

Each layer targets a different potential confound.

Interpretation Guidance

Statistical outputs are intended as exploratory diagnostics rather than definitive hypothesis tests. Results indicate structured differences that warrant deeper formal analysis.

Recommended Reporting

When presenting results, report window definitions, tolerances, null generation settings, Monte Carlo parameters, and classifier evaluation methodology to ensure interpretability.
